Decline export indices from 2^18 on in --cfg fuzzing builds

The parser's name/level/expression tables are dense vectors that grow up
to each record's "in"/"il"/"ie" index. The arena requires skipped and
out-of-order indices to be accepted, and trimmed exports keep large
original indices, so upstream has no bound: one record with
"in":444444445 makes a 16 KB input allocate a 3.5 GB table (3 s
natively; on wasm32 a raw_vec "capacity overflow" panic). Fuzzing builds
decline indices >= 2^18 (the largest in the arena and nano-lean fixtures
is far below that; kiota's trimmed fixtures reach 145684), which keeps
each table at a few MB. Repro in suite-repros.
Upstream: none (no related issue or PR, checked 2026-11-22).

